{
  "title": "8W8",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "TR-808 style drum",
        "machine. 16 voices,",
        "all synthesized,",
        "no samples.",
        "",
        "Kick, snare, toms,",
        "congas and clap are",
        "circuit models. The",
        "rest are checked",
        "against sc808 to",
        "within -64 dB."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Pads (left 4x4):",
        " r1: BD SD LT MT",
        " r2: HT LC MC HC",
        " r3: RS CL MA CP",
        " r4: CB CH OH CY",
        "",
        "16 drums, so no",
        "Master pad - reach",
        "it with the jog.",
        "Shift+Pad: select",
        " without sounding.",
        "Mute+Pad: mute that",
        " drum ([M] in bar)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Editing",
      "lines": [
        "Knobs 1-8 edit the",
        "page on screen.",
        "Jog: next page.",
        "Shift+Jog: jump",
        " section.",
        "Jog click: section",
        " list.",
        "Shift: show values",
        " and fine mode.",
        "Mute+knob: reset",
        " that pot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Kick Engine",
      "lines": [
        "Circ: the real 808",
        "circuit. DECAY is",
        "LOOP GAIN, not a",
        "time - the pitch",
        "sighs down and fast",
        "repeats never",
        "machine-gun.",
        "ATTACK is the",
        "beater click into",
        "the output.",
        "sc808: a sine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Snare Engine",
      "lines": [
        "Circ: two ringing",
        "shells at 173 and",
        "336 Hz, from the",
        "service notes.",
        " SNAPPY sets the",
        " noise length as",
        " well as its level.",
        " Tune moves both",
        " shells together.",
        "sc808: two sines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tom/Conga Eng",
      "lines": [
        "Circ: one bridged-T",
        "ringing in a loop,",
        "Q 10.8 from the",
        "service notes.",
        "DECAY is SECONDS of",
        "ring, solved into",
        "loop gain at the",
        "current pitch.",
        "Toms: noise head.",
        "Congas: clean, an",
        "octave up, longer.",
        "sc808: a sine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Clap Engine",
      "lines": [
        "Circ: three noise",
        "bursts ~10 ms apart",
        "then a 330 ms tail",
        "(R362 x C143),",
        "through the 874 Hz",
        "bandpass R342/R334",
        "make.",
        "",
        "DECAY is the tail.",
        "Burst and mix are",
        "the hardware's own.",
        "sc808: two bursts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Metal",
      "lines": [
        "On Master. How the",
        "hats' and cymbal's",
        "six oscillators",
        "behave between hits.",
        "",
        "Free: as the 808 -",
        " they never stop,",
        " so no two hits",
        " are the same.",
        "Retrig: as sc808 -",
        " identical hits."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Voices",
      "lines": [
        "Every drum has Tune,",
        "Decay, Drive, a",
        "Distortion type and",
        "Level. Defaults are",
        "the sc808 sound, not",
        "pot centre - except",
        "where a circuit",
        "engine is default,",
        "and there the",
        "default is what the",
        "hardware does.",
        "",
        "Rim and Clave have",
        "a pad each."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choke",
      "lines": [
        "The 808 shares one",
        "metal source between",
        "the hats, so closed",
        "cuts open. Here it",
        "is a switch:",
        " Off / CH>OH /",
        " Mutual.",
        "On the Closed Hat",
        "page and on Master."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Distortion",
      "lines": [
        "Per drum and across",
        "the kit: Diode,",
        "Clip, Fold, Crush.",
        "Same four as 9W9",
        "and 6W6, so the",
        "knob means the same",
        "thing on all three.",
        "",
        "Master Dist has an",
        "Off position."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Sequencing",
      "lines": [
        "Use Move's own",
        "sequencer: a drum",
        "track with a kit,",
        "muted (HiJack),",
        "track MIDI OUT on",
        "the slot's channel.",
        "",
        "Notes 36-50, one",
        "lane per drum, or",
        "General MIDI -",
        "switch on Master."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Accent",
      "lines": [
        "Velocity 100 and up",
        "gets the Accent",
        "multiplier, on the",
        "Master page.",
        "",
        "On the circuit kick",
        "and snare it is a",
        "trigger VOLTAGE, so",
        "a hard hit is a",
        "different sound and",
        "not just a louder."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Remote panel",
      "lines": [
        "A full 808 panel in",
        "a browser: every",
        "instrument at once,",
        "as columns.",
        "",
        "Port 7700 then",
        "/remote-ui, while",
        "8W8 is the slot's",
        "synth.",
        " move.local:7700",
        " 172.16.254.1:7700"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
